("perror","void perror(const char *s);","Writes an error message for errno to stderr.","If s is not NULL and not empty it is written first, followed by a colon and a blank, then the text of strerror(errno) and a newline.","Nothing.","strerror errno",None),
("printf","int printf(const char *format, ...);","Writes formatted output to stdout.","Characters of format are copied to the output, except conversion specifications that start with %, which format the following arguments. See {printf formats} for the flags, width, precision, length modifiers and conversions.","The number of characters written, or a negative value on error.","fprintf sprintf vprintf puts","#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void)\n{\n    int n = 42;\n    double x = 3.14159;\n    printf(\"%5d|%-5d|%05d\\n\", n, n, n);\n    printf(\"%8.3f|%e|%g\\n\", x, x, x);\n    printf(\"%s has %d chars\\n\", \"text\", 4);\n    return 0;\n}"),
("putc","int putc(int c, FILE *stream);","Writes a character to a stream.","Same as fputc; it may be implemented as a macro, so the arguments must not have side effects.","The character written, or EOF on error.","fputc putchar",None),
("putchar","int putchar(int c);","Writes a character to stdout.","Same as putc(c, stdout).","The character written, or EOF on error.","putc puts printf",None),
